<body>
<main>
<h1>chi-server Onboarding</h1>
<p class="muted">Server: <code>__HOST__</code> · generated __GENERATED__ · this page only opens while you are connected to Tailscale</p>
<nav><a href="#apps">What's here</a><a href="#iphone">iPhone</a><a href="#mac">MacBook</a><a href="#android">Android</a><a href="#cn">China-only content</a><a href="#rules">House rules</a><a href="#help">Troubleshooting</a></nav>

<h2 id="apps">What you can use</h2>
<div class="card"><table>
<tr><th>Service</th><th>Open</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
<tr><td>Home</td><td><a href="https://__FQDN__">Open ↗</a></td><td>Entry point for every service</td></tr>
<tr><td>Jellyfin</td><td><a href="https://__FQDN__:8009">:8009 ↗</a></td><td>Media library. Ask the admin for an account</td></tr>
<tr><td>MeTube</td><td><a href="https://__FQDN__:8010">:8010 ↗</a></td><td>Paste a video link -> it downloads into the media library (if the admin enabled it for you)</td></tr>
<tr><td>AI chat</td><td><a href="https://__FQDN__:8003">:8003 ↗</a></td><td>Local LLM. After you sign up, wait for the admin to approve you (if enabled)</td></tr>
<tr><td>China proxy</td><td><a href="#cn">Setup</a></td><td>See "China-only content" below</td></tr>
</table></div>
<p class="muted">Every address has the form <code>https://__FQDN__:port</code>. If a service does not load, the admin has not shared it with you or it is not enabled. Just ask the admin.</p>

<h2 id="iphone">iPhone / iPad</h2>
<h3>1. Connect to the server (required)</h3>
<ol>
<li>Install <b>Tailscale</b> from the App Store and sign in with any account (Google / Apple / Microsoft).</li>
<li>Open the <b>invite link</b> the admin sent you and accept it. You should then see <code>__HOST__</code> in Tailscale.</li>
<li>Turn Tailscale on (it shows Connected). You can turn it off when not in use; it only carries traffic to the server and does not affect the rest of your browsing.</li>
<li>Open the <a href="https://__FQDN__">home page</a> in Safari -> Share -> <b>Add to Home Screen</b>. From then on, just tap the icon.</li>
</ol>
<h3>2. Watch the media library</h3>
<ul>
<li>Install <b>Swiftfin</b> (the official native Jellyfin client for iOS, free) or <b>Jellyfin Mobile</b> from the App Store.</li>
<li>Server address: <code>https://__FQDN__:8009</code>. Ask the admin for a username and password.</li>
<li>To watch on a TV: tap AirPlay in the player, or use the Jellyfin app on the TV box at home.</li>
</ul>
<h3>3. Send a video to the server with one tap (optional, needs MeTube access)</h3>
<ol>
<li>Open the <b>Shortcuts</b> app -> <b>+</b> (top right) -> name it "Save to chi".</li>
<li>Tap ⓘ at the bottom -> turn on <b>Show in Share Sheet</b>, and accept only <b>URLs</b>.</li>
<li>Add the action <b>Get Contents of URL</b>: URL <code>https://__FQDN__:8010/add</code>; expand it -> Method <b>POST</b>; Request Body <b>JSON</b>; add the fields <code>url</code> = <i>Shortcut Input</i> and <code>quality</code> = <code>1080</code>.</li>
<li>Add the action <b>Show Notification</b>: "Sent to chi".</li>
<li>From now on, in the YouTube / Bilibili app tap Share -> More -> "Save to chi". A few minutes later it shows up in Jellyfin.</li>
</ol>

<h2 id="mac">MacBook</h2>
<h3>1. Connect to the server (required)</h3>
<ol>
<li>Install <b>Tailscale</b> from the Mac App Store or <a href="https://tailscale.com/download/mac">tailscale.com/download/mac</a>. Sign in, then open and accept the admin's invite link.</li>
<li>Open the <a href="https://__FQDN__">home page</a> in your browser and bookmark it.</li>
</ol>
<h3>2. Watch the media library</h3>
<ul>
<li>Open <a href="https://__FQDN__:8009">Jellyfin</a> in the browser, or install the desktop client: <code>brew install --cask jellyfin-media-player</code> (server: <code>https://__FQDN__:8009</code>).</li>
</ul>
<h3>3. SSH (admins only)</h3>
<p><code>ssh &lt;user&gt;@__HOST__</code></p>

<h2 id="android">Android</h2>
<ul>
<li>Install <b>Tailscale</b> from the Play Store, sign in, accept the invite link.</li>
<li>Install <b>Jellyfin</b> from the Play Store; server <code>https://__FQDN__:8009</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="cn">Mainland-China-only content (Bilibili / iQIYI / Tencent Video)</h2>
<p>The server runs a China-exit proxy: only these mainland video sites go through the China route; every other site is unaffected. Your device just needs to use the proxy for those sites, and the <b>PAC URL</b> below decides that automatically.</p>
<div class="card"><p>PAC URL: <code>https://__FQDN__:8008/chi.pac</code></p></div>
<h3>MacBook (works best, from anywhere)</h3>
<ol>
<li>System Settings -> Network -> Wi-Fi -> <b>Details...</b> next to the current network -> <b>Proxies</b>.</li>
<li>Turn on <b>Automatic proxy configuration</b>, paste the PAC URL above -> OK.</li>
<li>Stay connected to Tailscale. bilibili.com in Safari / Chrome now shows the mainland version.</li>
<li>To stop, turn "Automatic proxy configuration" off. On wired Ethernet, repeat the same steps under Ethernet.</li>
</ol>
<h3>iPhone</h3>
<ol>
<li>Settings -> Wi-Fi -> ⓘ next to the current network -> <b>Configure Proxy</b> (at the bottom) -> <b>Automatic</b> -> paste the PAC URL.</li>
<li>Stay connected to Tailscale and open the Bilibili app.</li>
</ol>
<div class="warn"><b>Limitations:</b> iPhone proxy settings are <b>per Wi-Fi network</b>, so there is no way to set one on cellular. Also, iOS runs only one VPN-type app at a time, and with Tailscale on there is no guarantee every app honors the PAC - try it, and if it does not work, watch on a Mac.</div>
<h3>TV box / projector at home</h3>
<p>The admin has already set this up on the server; just use the Bilibili TV app or BBLL on the box.</p>

<h2 id="rules">House rules</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Your invite link is for you only</b> - do not forward it. Every guest gets their own invite.</li>
<li>Disk space is limited (the download area is capped at __MEDIA_MAX_GB__ GB, and the oldest files are deleted when it fills up). Ask the admin to move anything you want to keep into Keep.</li>
<li>The China route is paid traffic: watching is fine, bulk downloading through it is not.</li>
<li>Only download things you will watch yourself; do not use it to redistribute content.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="help">Troubleshooting</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Nothing opens</b> -> Is Tailscale Connected? Can you see <code>__HOST__</code> in Tailscale?</li>
<li><b>The browser shows a certificate error</b> -> Use the full <code>__FQDN__</code> address, not an IP.</li>
<li><b>Bilibili still says the content is region-locked</b> -> Check the PAC URL and that Tailscale is connected; if it still fails, tell the admin.</li>
<li>Anything else: ask the admin.</li>
</ul>
